1
00:00:00,686 --> 00:00:02,586
(Amy:)I think it'll be fine.

2
00:00:03,639 --> 00:00:05,239
(Sheldon:)Very well, then.

3
00:00:05,307 --> 00:00:07,577
(Sheldon:)I'll see you
on Thanksgiving morning.

4
00:00:07,643 --> 00:00:09,373
(Amy:)See you then.
Oh,

5
00:00:09,445 --> 00:00:11,845
(Sheldon:)and forget what I said
about the Myanmar catfish.

6
00:00:11,914 --> 00:00:15,254
(Sheldon:)My list of marine-themed
pilgrim facts is pretty short.

7
00:00:15,317 --> 00:00:17,457
(Amy:)Did you know they served
shellfish and eel

8
00:00:17,519 --> 00:00:18,759
(Amy:)at the very first Thanksgiving?

9
00:00:18,787 --> 00:00:21,187
(Sheldon:)And there goes my list.

10
00:00:23,792 --> 00:00:25,862
(Emily:)So, how does this work?

11
00:00:25,928 --> 00:00:28,328
(Bernadette:)The soup kitchen manager
assigns the jobs,

12
00:00:28,397 --> 00:00:30,297
(Bernadette:)and the shifts
are six hours.

13
00:00:30,365 --> 00:00:31,435
(Howard:)Six hours?

14
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:34,940
(Howard:)Oh, God, I don't want to
complain for that long.

15
00:00:35,904 --> 00:00:38,304
(Raj:)Do you ever do anything
for anyone else?

16
00:00:38,373 --> 00:00:43,913
(Howard:)I happen to be
a giving and generous lover.

17
00:00:43,979 --> 00:00:47,149
(Emily:)Are you and I close enough
for me to say that's creepy?

18
00:00:47,216 --> 00:00:51,256
(Bernadette:)We are, and I believe the word
you're looking for is... yech!

19
00:00:52,454 --> 00:00:53,884
(Soup Kitchen Manager:)Uh, can I help you?

20
00:00:53,956 --> 00:00:55,726
(Bernadette:)Hi. We'd like to volunteer.

21
00:00:55,791 --> 00:00:57,491
(Soup Kitchen Manager:)Oh, I appreciate
you guys coming down,

22
00:00:57,559 --> 00:00:58,889
(Soup Kitchen Manager:)but we already have
enough people.

23
00:00:58,961 --> 00:01:00,661
(Soup Kitchen Manager:)Any other day,
please, come back.

